---
import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
---

<InfoLayout
  eyebrow="Tooling"
  title="Slack"
  description="Where the actual project conversation happens — and where these skills go looking for what to log."
>
  <p>
    Every project runs in its own Slack channel. That's where meetings get scheduled, decisions
    get made mid-thread, and documents get shared without anyone stopping to log them anywhere
    else. Several of the skills on this site exist specifically to catch what that produces before
    it scrolls away.
  </p>

  <h2>The weekly rhythm</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/#tab-cadence">Meeting Recap</a> reconciles a PM's own notes against the Gemini/AI
    notes and transcript, then posts the result as a threaded reply under that meeting's agenda
    message. <a href="/#tab-cadence">Slack/Notion Sync</a> mines that exact recap for decisions,
    risks, and action items and writes them into the Project Workbook the same day.
  </p>

  <h2>What a recap alone misses</h2>
  <p>
    A recap only covers what got flagged in the meeting itself. <a href="/#tab-cadence">Link
    Harvest</a> covers the rest — sweeping a channel over a date range, reading every thread in
    full, for documents that were shared but never made it into any recap.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
